A client holds the old cluster object of a node that missed ALTER CLUSTER ADD (DEBUG WAIT without a timeout): the first rejoin attempt fails before it connects, the second one after a pause succeeds.
––– block: ../base/replication/rejoin-setup –––
––– comment –––
The waiter takes a reference to the cluster object on node 3 and never gets its commit
––– input –––
(mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "debug wait v1 status 1000" > /dev/null 2>&1 &); sleep 1; echo "waiter started"
––– output –––
waiter started
––– block: ../base/replication/rejoin-pause-node3 –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "CREATE TABLE t1 (title text, v int)"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "INSERT INTO t1 (id,title,v) VALUES (1,'x',1)"; timeout 60 mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "ALTER CLUSTER v1 ADD t1"; echo $?
––– output –––
0
––– input –––
LC=$(mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE 'cluster_v1_last_committed'\G" | awk '/Value:/{print $2}'); kill -CONT $P3; echo "node 3 resumed"
––– output –––
node 3 resumed
––– input –––
timeout 60 bash -c 'v() { mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE '\''cluster_v1_$1'\''\G" | awk "/Value:/{print \$2}"; }; until [ "$(v node_state)" = synced ] && [ "$(v last_committed)" = "'$LC'" ]; do sleep 0.5; done'; echo "synced $?"
––– output –––
synced 0
––– input –––
kill -0 $P3 && echo alive; for t in t0 t1; do echo "$t $(mysql -h0 -P3306 -N -e "SELECT id FROM $t" | grep -Eo "[0-9]+" | sort -n | xargs)"; done
––– output –––
alive
t0 1
t1 1
––– comment –––
Attempt 1 times out waiting for the old object, attempt 2 starts after the retry pause and joins by SST
––– input –––
L=/var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log; chk() { grep -q -- "$2" $L && echo "yes: $1" || echo "no: $1"; }; chk 'attempt 1' "rejoin by SST, attempt 1 of 2"; chk 'attempt 1 failed' "rejoin attempt 1 failed: previous cluster object still in use"; chk 'attempt 2' "rejoin by SST, attempt 2 of 2"; chk 'attempt 2 started' "rejoin started, attempt 2"; chk 'gave up' "failed 2 times"; grep -c 'CRASH DUMP' $L; grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok' $L
––– output –––
yes: attempt 1
yes: attempt 1 failed
yes: attempt 2
yes: attempt 2 started
no: gave up
0
1
